LOCATION: town

OBJECT: gazette
  GATE: evidence(gazette_correction_printed)
  LABEL: "Read the morning paper"
  THE GAZETTE: "TRAGEDY AT THE OPHION CLUB\n\nFive names. Five professions.\nA paragraph about service to the community."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The birches do not appear in the account.\nNeither does a source for the word accident."
  THE CORRECTION SLIP: "A later printed slip records the police count of eight and names Naomi with its identification sources. The correction supplements the morning edition; it does not replace the copies already sold."
  NOTEBOOK: gazette_slip_note | "The paper names five club members and describes an apparent accident. It names neither the woman nor the boy. Its report supplies no independent explanation of the wounds."
  EVIDENCE: gazette

OBJECT: gazette
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Read the morning paper"
  THE GAZETTE: "TRAGEDY AT THE OPHION CLUB\n\nFive names. Five professions.\nA paragraph about service to the community."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The birches do not appear in the account.\nNeither does a source for the word accident."
  NOTEBOOK: gazette_note | "The paper names five club members and describes an apparent accident. It names neither the woman nor the boy. Its report supplies no independent explanation of the wounds."
  EVIDENCE: gazette

OBJECT: lodging
  GATE: evidence(naomi)
  LABEL: "Examine the meal ledger"
  THE MEAL LEDGER: "N. FREEMAN — TWO MEALS.\n\nA small balance carried forward.\nA line in a book kept for an ordinary purpose."
  MRS. ALMY: "Hers. And the boy's.\n\nThe balance can wait."
  WALTER'S NOTEBOOK: "Copy the entry and record its source.\nThe name and the address corroborate her statement.\n\nFor once, a question has produced exactly what the work needed."
  NOTEBOOK: lodging_note | "The boardinghouse meal ledger records N. Freeman and a boy. Mrs. Almy confirms the entry. They were known locally; the record supplies a place from which to continue the inquiry."
  EVIDENCE: lodging

OBJECT: lodging
  GATE: NOT evidence(naomi)
  LABEL: "Examine the meal ledger"
  A PRIVATE LEDGER: "Ask Mrs. Almy whose entry you are looking for before copying her book."

OBJECT: exemption
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Examine the folded notice"
  THE DRESSER: "An exemption notice, folded along the same worn crease.\nConstance Corwin's name beneath his own.\nBeside it, in the half-open drawer: a tin of menthol ointment dried to dark resin, and three folded gauze masks with brittle, yellowed ties.\n\nWalter puts the notice back.\nThere are other papers requiring him tonight."
  NOTEBOOK: exemption_note | "Walter's old exemption notice records the need to care for Constance Corwin. It concerns his life before the case. It supplies no evidence about the deaths at the estate."
  EVIDENCE: exemption

OBJECT: morgue_tables
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Examine the tables"
  THE TABLES: "Six tables. Four newer than the others, the enamel still bright. The county put them in during the autumn of '18 and never took them out."